body:
Scope boundary (prose; assessed by review): this change-set's surfaces are:

(a) the plan-verify derived-coverage scope computation and the tests that pin it;

(b) the agent-prompt coverage rule: `opencode-suite/agents/plan-review.md` verifies coverage DETERMINISTICALLY via the binary's delta coverage check and treats any gap as blocking feedback, then reviews each plan node semantically against the spec delta with a less-code bias (removing a solution node / `implemented-by` edge normally yields a `deletes` task; a keep/modify must be justified in a task note); `opencode-suite/agents/implementation-phase-reviewer.md` states the delta coverage rule — in that statement only, with no other change to that agent;

(c) the spec-principles prompt surfaces (`requirements.requirement.durable-spec-states-what-is`): every distributed writer prompt — `opencode-suite/agents/spec-writer.md`, `plan-writer.md`, `codebase-navigator.md` — carries the writer rules (author target truth only; a superseded statement is updated or removed, never annotated; no rejected alternatives, change-logs, or decision/reconciliation/correction/provenance notes; a `note` deepens understanding of what is only), and every distributed reviewer prompt — `spec-review.md`, `plan-review.md`, `implementation-phase-reviewer.md` — carries the reviewer rules (review every changed spec node against the principles; raise blocking feedback on history content; the fix is delete/rewrite, never annotate).

All six prompts are product source (`solution.constraint.suite-is-product-source`), embedded via `include_str!` and installed by `apg init`; the repo's own `.opencode/agents/**` remain consumer artifacts and are not edited here.

The change-set does NOT change the planned-node realization gate, the feedback-resolution gate, the durable node/edge write surface, the suite tools (`apg_plan_*` — including `apg_plan_phases`'s own project/requirement scoping), or `apg plan verify`'s CLI/exit surface; the coverage refusal keeps naming the owning solution node and the uncovered code FQN. The spec-principles surface is prompt-only: no seeded global constraint, no binary change, no lint.
